; A windtrap suite over the mutation runtime. The runtime's independence
; from the windtrap core is a property of lib/mutate; the suite itself
; dogfoods windtrap. arm_child stands in for an instrumented executable,
; exercising registration, arming from WINDTRAP_MUTATE_ARM, the runaway
; budget and the atomic verdict write end to end in a separate process.
; Nothing here writes under _build/_mutants: every path the suite writes
; to lives in a private scratch directory removed at exit.

(executable
 (name arm_child)
 (modules arm_child)
 (libraries windtrap_mutate))

; The negative control for the mutation seam: a suite that links windtrap
; and not windtrap.mutation, so the registry's slot is empty and a
; WINDTRAP_MUTATE ask has no interceptor to answer it. The driver must
; refuse to start rather than run as if nothing was asked; unset, the run
; is an ordinary one.

(executable
 (name unlinked_main)
 (modules unlinked_main)
 (libraries windtrap))

(test
 (name test_mutate)
 (modules test_mutate)
 (libraries windtrap windtrap_mutate unix)
 (deps arm_child.exe unlinked_main.exe))
